"use strict";exports.id=2190,exports.ids=[2190],exports.modules={2190:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"page_label":"How to invest","page_title":"Investment strategies","page_intro":"These are the most common approaches for buying bitcoin. Pick the one that fits your personality and your situation.","guides_label":"Before you start","guides_title":"Investment guides","guides_intro":"A few simple principles that will save you money, anxiety, and regrets. Read these before anything else.","guide_sleep_title":"Sleep on it","guide_sleep_text":"If an investment keeps you up at night or makes you anxious, it\'s too much for you right now. Protecting your peace is also a strategy.","guide_lose_title":"Only invest money you can afford to lose","guide_lose_text":"Base your investment on potential losses, not gains. Never invest money meant for rent, food, or bills.","guide_vote_title":"Investing is a vote","guide_vote_text":"Where you put your money is a statement. Invest in what you believe in. Money invested in war fuels war. Money invested in clean energy fuels clean energy.","guide_time_title":"Time beats timing","guide_time_text":"Nobody knows the highs and lows. Invest regularly, wait patiently, and let your money work for you.","strat_a_title":"DCA \xb7 Dollar Cost Averaging","strat_a_subtitle":"The beginner\'s best friend","strat_a_badge":"Recommended","strat_a_body_1":"Pick a fixed affordable monthly amount (e.g. 50€). Buy bitcoin with it every month, same day, regardless of price. Some months you get more bitcoin, some less — it evens out over time.","strat_a_body_2":"No market knowledge needed. Just patience and discipline. Hold for 5+ years.","strat_a_tip":"Be boring about it. Set a reminder, buy, and move on. Don\'t check the price every day.","strat_b_title":"Weighted DCA \xb7 DCA v2","strat_b_subtitle":"Same idea, smarter execution","strat_b_badge":"Intermediate","strat_b_body_1":"Same as DCA but adapt the monthly amount based on market conditions. Set a range (e.g. 0€–100€/month). When bitcoin looks cheap — based on signals like RSI under 30, fear in the market, or few addresses in profit — invest more. When bitcoin is breaking records, invest less.","strat_b_body_2":"In deep crashes, temporarily increase significantly using spare investment funds — not emergency money. Don\'t aim for the exact bottom.","strat_b_metrics_link":"Metrics page","strat_b_tip":"You\'re not timing the market — just being smart about how much you put in.","strat_c_title":"Lump-Sum \xb7 All-in at the lows","strat_c_subtitle":"High risk, high reward — not for beginners","strat_c_badge":"Advanced","strat_c_body_1":"Wait for a major crash, then invest a large amount at once. Great in theory, very hard emotionally in practice. Requires knowing at least one full bitcoin cycle (~4 years).","strat_c_body_2":"Without experience, it\'s easy to buy too early, panic sell, or miss the window. This is closer to trading than investing — look for dedicated courses outside this page if you want to learn it.","strat_c_tip":"Most people are better off with DCA. Lump-sum sounds great in hindsight, but it\'s brutal in real time.","strat_d_title":"Gold \xb7 The classic safe haven","strat_d_subtitle":"For those who prefer stability over volatility","strat_d_badge":"Alternative","strat_d_body_1":"If bitcoin feels too volatile, that\'s valid — but doing nothing isn\'t safe either. Inflation quietly erodes your savings every year. Gold has been a trusted store of value for thousands of years.","strat_d_body_2":"Buy physical gold as a hedge. For details on how to invest in gold, look for platforms specialized in that.","strat_d_tip":"That said — keep at least a little bitcoin. You know why \uD83D\uDE09","metrics_link_text":"Metrics page"}')}};